    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116837,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>When Bloom syndrome is clinically suspected, the detection of biallelic pathogenic variants in the <em>BLM</em> gene and/or the identification of an increased frequency of sister-chromatid exchanges in specialized cytogenetic studies may help establish the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T15:42:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 116838,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 317,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> clinical features including small size and distinctive facial features; <em>BLM</em> mutation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-02T15:42:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
